On Monday 24 May 2004 00:37 Gordon Ingram (ggi@st-andrews.ac.uk) wrote:

> In the latest of my "questions I can't find the answer to anywhere",
> I'd like to know how to designate a weapon as the secondary one,
> without having the option set that shoves the one that was in hand
> into the secondary position when you change weapon. Any takers?

You have 'pushweapon' off, right?

Wield the weapon you want as secondary. Press 'x'. This puts the weapon
in your off hand. You can now wield your primary weapon in your primary
hand. Change weapons with 'x' as often as you like (I use it for a
dagger and a pick-axe when playing P, for instance).

   Raisse, killed by a dagger

